# Planned city upgrade validation

Require construction-plan cities to upgrade an owned settlement.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] A planned city is valid on an existing settlement belonging to the selected player.
- [x] A planned city is valid on that player's settlement created by an earlier valid plan step.
- [x] A planned city is invalid on an empty vertex, an existing city, or another player's settlement.
- [x] An invalid city attempt does not append or mutate any plan step or real Board state.
- [x] Preview projection upgrades the settlement to a ghost city without retaining a duplicate settlement.
- [x] Board edit-mode building cycling remains unchanged unless separately required.
- [x] Invalid attempts use TASK-019's shared 1.5-second lower-screen feedback.
- [x] Analytical domain tests and UI regression coverage compile.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- Ordered projection must validate against the Board plus all earlier accepted plan steps.

## Evidence

- Added `cityNeedsSettlement` domain validation with exact feedback for empty vertices, existing cities, and opponent settlements.
- Kept Board cycling behavior unchanged: an empty Board vertex still begins as a settlement, while explicit plan-city placement must upgrade an owned settlement.
- Added analytical tests for valid/invalid ownership cases and sequential projection of settlement then city into one city.
- Added UI coverage confirming an invalid empty-vertex city produces feedback and appends no plan step.
- The complete app and test bundles compile using `/private/tmp/Catanalyst-tasks018-024-derived`.
